  "pop_behind_why_none": "cutout law 16 keys the crossing to a beat where he NAMES the tool.  This take names three - Codex 8.38, Claude Cowork 9.14, Grok Build 10.06 - and at each of those instants that tool's own mark is ALREADY on the STAGE in its 112 px tile.  ROUND-2/3 law 6 keeps the story's own subject mark out of the depth field (which is why the plan's cutout_logo_lanes name six neighbours and none of the three), so a crossing here would be either the same mark twice in one instant or a mark he never names.  Nothing else in the take is a mark: AI, RAM, CPU and 'processes' are categories.  The plan declares no window; the handoff's SS5.7 offers the tile arrivals as a seat without asking for one, and that seat sits above the silhouette (lowest ink canvas 758, cap top ~845), so a card crossing there could never be occluded by him - which is the whole point of the detail.",
